<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fecht</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fecht is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, that rises in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a> and flows east through the Munster valley and Turckheim to join the Ill north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colmar">Colmar</a>. Its valley was long a route across the Vosges into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, and the abbey of Munster lay on its upper course.</p></div>
